CreateClass_Captable_Unit_Concrete_Test
├── when the caller is not the company Governor
│   ├── given the caller is the Safe
│   │   └── it should revert with OnlyGovernor
│   └── given the caller is anyone else
│       └── it should revert with OnlyGovernor
└── when the caller is the company Governor
    ├── when the company already has 32 classes
    │   └── it should revert with TooManyClasses
    ├── given the company has 31 classes
    │   └── it should create the 32nd class
    ├── when the authorised amount is 0
    │   └── it should revert with InvalidClass
    ├── when convertsInto names a missing class or the class itself
    │   └── it should revert with InvalidClass
    ├── when a class with no issue price has a preference
    │   └── it should revert with InvalidClass
    ├── when a priced class has a floor of 0 or above its issue price
    │   └── it should revert with InvalidClass
    ├── when the rule is Custom and the rule contract is the zero address
    │   └── it should revert with InvalidClass
    ├── when weight times authorised times the highest ratio is above the vote bound
    │   └── it should revert with VotesBoundExceeded
    ├── when the authorised amount would break the target class's reserve
    │   └── it should revert with AuthorisedExceeded
    └── when the class is valid
        ├── it should deploy a ShareClass clone with the name and ticker
        ├── it should store the weight and terms and transfer rule
        ├── it should set the first conversion price to the original issue price
        ├── given the class converts into another
        │   └── it should add its reserve rounded up to the target's convertible reserve
        ├── given the convertible class has no issue price
        │   └── it should reserve one target share per authorised share
        ├── it should return the next class id
        └── it should emit ClassCreated
